DESCRIPTION:In celebration of beloved author and illustrator Virginia Lee 
 Burton—and in honor of the upcoming anniversary of her August 31st birth
 day—the Cape Ann Museum is pleased to partner with the Sawyer Free Libra
 ry and 1623 Studios on a special screening of the award‑winning document
 ary Virginia Lee Burton: A Sense of Place\, produced by Christine Lundberg
 . The screening will take place on August 28th at 3:00 p.m. in the Communi
 ty Room of the Sawyer Free Library. Martha Oaks\, CAM’s Chief Curator\, 
 will offer introductory remarks\, reflecting on Burton’s enduring legacy
  and her deep connections to Cape Ann’s artistic and cultural landscape.
 \n\nSources: North of Boston\nEvent page: https://northofboston.org/event/
 community-program-documentary-screening-a-sense-of-place/
