BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Pastel Workshop: The Nature of Color with Kimberly Jermain
DTSTART:20260912T103000
DTEND:20260912T123000
DTSTAMP:20260827T212256Z
UID:8b22241f7dc85400e32e5dfe6c38ac@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Discover the power of color in the natural world during this t
 wo-hour outdoor workshop led by artist and author Kimberly Collins Jermain
 . Set on the CAM Green\, this hands-on session introduces participants to 
 working with pastel through an exercise from Jermain’s newly published b
 ook The Nature of Color\, which presents her innovative\, nature-based app
 roach to understanding and using color in art. Note: Materials included. C
 lass time is primarily outdoors\; please dress appropriately for the weath
 er. Kimberly Collins Jermain is a landscape painter\, teacher\, and archit
 ectural color designer whose work uses the power of color to change how we
  experience the world. Since 1989\, Kimberly has collaborated with over 80
 0 clients\, including homeowners\, architects\, interior designers\, devel
 opers\, and commercial property owners on color design projects.\n\nSource
 s: North of Boston\nEvent page: https://northofboston.org/event/pastel-wor
 kshop-the-nature-of-color-with-kimberly-jermain/
LOCATION:Cape Ann Museum Green\, 13 Poplar Street\, Gloucester\, MA\, 0193
 0
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/pastel-workshop-the-nature-of-color-wi
 th-kimberly-jermain/
