BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Ana Popovic with Danielle Miraglia
DTSTART:20260926T200000
DTEND:20260926T220000
DTSTAMP:20260827T212256Z
UID:763902ea04c81b34be4798ab50efb7@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:“In the 25 years since the release of her debut record\, Hom
 etown\, tail-gunning blues virtuoso Ana Popovic has proved herself a force
  of nature with a vintage Stratin hand.” – Guitar World “Ana Popovic
  Melds Rock\, Blues\, and Jazz for Fiery Power” – No Depression “A b
 adass with a silver Strat\, she performs the heck out of this song [“Wor
 ked Up”]\, owning it with swagger and grace. … “Worked Up” capture
 s her love of funky grooves plus the edginess of rocking guitar power. –
  Rock & Blues Muse Los Angeles-based and critically acclaimed guitarist an
 d singer Ana Popovic is set to release her highly anticipated album Dance 
 To The Rhythm (Electric Heel Records) on September 26\, 2025. Produced by 
 Popovic and Buthel\, the album showcases a groundbreaking fusion of groove
 \, blues\, funk\, and soul. Building on the success of her previous work\,
  Dance To The Rhythm pushes boundaries\, seamlessly blending infectious da
 nce grooves (“Dance To The Rhythm” / “Sho Nuff”) with raw blues gu
 itar and powerful lyrics. From the soulful “Soul’ution” to the funky
  “Hottest Ticket In Town” and the bluesy “Dwell On The Feeling”\, 
 “California Chase\,” the album weaves a rich tapestry of musical style
 s\, reflecting Popovic’s masterful versatility. The track “Sisters and
  Brothers” channels a Steely Dan-like arrangement\, while “Hurt So Goo
 d” brings a contemporary mainstream flair. The ultimate jam comes in the
  form of a clever reimagining of Paul Simon’s “50 Ways to Leave Your L
 over.” Ana says: “One of my biggest strengths on stage is my ability t
 o make people dance. Music should take you to a place where you can let go
 \, feel the groove\, and move. You want music to grab you\, to have a pock
 et that you can’t resist. —everything else revolves around it. Blues g
 uitar has never really been part of dance music before\, and in that way\,
  it’s revolutionary. Guitar plays a central role in these tracks\, break
 ing down the boundaries created by time\, culture\, and musical traditions
 . With this album\, I’m pushing those boundaries.” For Ana\, blues gui
 tar is the foundation of everything in her music. Yet\, she masterfully bl
 ends genres\, effortlessly shifting from blues to dance\, jam band\, funk
 \, pop\, and even gospel—it’s all part of her evolving sound. A true p
 ioneer\, Ana combines her blues guitar roots with bold experimentation\, r
 edefining the intersection of blues and dance music. Her live performances
 \, whether with her six-piece or eleven-piece funk band FUNTASTAFUNK\, are
  electrifying\, blending fierce guitar work with irresistible rhythms that
  compel audiences to move. A multi-award-winning artist\, Popovic has earn
 ed recognition from major outlets and industry figures\, including Bruce S
 pringsteen\, who called her “one helluva guitar player.” She’s been 
 nominated for seven Blues Music Awards\, and her latest album POWER hit #1
  on the Billboard Blues Chart. Ana has shared stages with legends such as 
 B.B. King\, Joe Bonamassa\, Warren Haynes\, Robert Plant\, and Gary Clark 
 Jr.\, and is an endorsee of Fender\, D’Angelico\, Jim Dunlop\, and DR St
 rings. Popovic’s commitment to her craft and fearless boundary-pushing e
 nsures she remains one of the most dynamic forces in contemporary blues an
 d beyond. Danielle Miraglia Danielle Miraglia (murr-Ä L e a) comes armed 
 with a strong steady thumb on an old Gibson\,an infectious stomp-box rhyth
 m\, harmonica and tunes ranging from heart-felt to socially conscious that
  will move both your heart and hips.\n\nSources: North of Boston\nEvent pa
 ge: https://northofboston.org/event/ana-popovic-with-danielle-miraglia/
LOCATION:The Cut\, 177 Main Street\, Gloucester\, MA\, 01930
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/ana-popovic-with-danielle-miraglia/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Cesar Orozco: Festival Latino
DTSTART:20260926T190000
DTEND:20260926T210000
DTSTAMP:20260827T212256Z
UID:198103df85573449aa855351e33989@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Cuban-Venezuelan musician César Orozco will perform a free co
 ncert at the Mahaiwe Performing Arts Center coinciding with the 30th Anniv
 ersary of Festival Latino of the Berkshires. Orozco will perform with his 
 new 8-piece band\, SonAhead. Advance registration is required. Registratio
 n is open now. This show is presented as part of the Mahaiwe’s Partnerin
 g with Latinx Communities Program in collaboration with SCAN (Spanish-lang
 uage Community Advisory Network). El músico cubano-venezolano César Oroz
 co ofrecerá un concierto gratuito en el Mahaiwe Performing Arts Center co
 incidiendo con el 30º aniversario del Festival Latino de los Berkshires. 
 Orozco actuará con su nueva banda de 8 músicos\, SonAhead. Se requiere i
 nscripción previa. Las inscripciones ya están abiertas. Este show se pre
 senta como parte del programa Asociación con Comunidades Latinx de Mahaiw
 e en colaboración con SCAN (Red de Asesores de la Comunidad de Habla Hisp
 ana).\n\nSources: The Berkshires\nEvent page: https://berkshires.org/event
 s-old/cesar-orozco-festival-latino/
LOCATION:Mahaiwe Performing Arts Center\, 14 Castle Street\, Great Barring
 ton\, MA\, 01230
URL:https://berkshires.org/events-old/cesar-orozco-festival-latino/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Chromatic Wood Type — Old and New Interactive Discussion at the 
 Museum of Printing
DTSTART:20260926T130000
DTEND:20260926T160000
DTSTAMP:20260827T212256Z
UID:a9cc570fec3c649573d9b87b1fd78a@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Geri McCormick and James Grieshaber will give an explanation o
 f chromatic wood type and how they have recreated the making process to re
 vive historic chromatic fonts at Virgin Wood Type in Rochester\, NY. Their
  rediscovery of the process has led to an all new design which debuted ear
 lier this year called Marquee. There will be an informal activity followin
 g the talk where attendees will be able to pull a proof of a historic Will
 iam H. Page chromatic wood type ca. 1849 and the new Marquee font from Vir
 gin Wood Type made just this year. About the Museum of Printing The Museum
  of Printing is a non-profit dedicated to preserving the rich history of t
 he graphic arts\, printing and typesetting technology\, and printing craft
 smanship. In addition to many special collections and small exhibits\, the
  Museum contains hundreds of antique printing\, typesetting\, and bindery 
 machines\, as well as a library of books and printing-related documents an
 d a recently added bible room. The Museum is located at 15 Thornton Avenue
  in Haverhill\, Massachusetts. You can find us on the web at museumofprint
 ing.org and follow our social media activity on Facebook ( TheMuseumofPrin
 ting )\, Instagram ( museumofprinting )\, Twitter ( @MOPrinting )\, Substa
 ck\, Bluesky ( @museumofprinting.bsky.social) \, and YouTube ( @museumofpr
 inting ).\n\nSources: North of Boston\nEvent page: https://northofboston.o
 rg/event/chromatic-wood-type-old-and-new-interactive-discussion-at-the-mus
 eum-of-printing/
LOCATION:Museum of Printing\, 15 Thornton Ave\, Haverhill\, MA\, 01832
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/chromatic-wood-type-old-and-new-intera
 ctive-discussion-at-the-museum-of-printing/
END:VEVENT
